ub.com/repos/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-A/statuses/00e2079fb16f665721bf6b0fb209f07d22e0906f"}}, "author_association": "OWNER", "auto_merge": null, "assignee": null, "active_lock_reason": null, "merged": false, "mergeable": true, "rebaseable": true, "mergeable_state": "clean", "merged_by": null, "comments": 1, "review_comments": 0, "maintainer_can_modify": false, "commits": 1, "additions": 403, "deletions": 0, "changed_files": 6}, "review": {"id": 5244965776, "node_id": "PRR_kwDOUJyJf88AAAABOJ_TkA", "user": {"login": "Dengnifer", "id": 89234078, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjg5MjM0MDc4", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/89234078?u=7a60297a751d9142f3705fd4d6c15e08cfe00d0f&v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer", "html_url": "https://github.com/Dengnifer", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "body": "<!-- mipstarre-review pr=595 head=00e2079fb16f665721bf6b0fb209f07d22e0906f -->\n# Independent review - PR 595 @ 00e2079fb16f665721bf6b0fb209f07d22e0906f\n\nreviewer_session: independent-gpt-5.6-sol-ultra-20260918\nci_status: success (nine exact-head contexts)\ntrusted_main: 7cfd9033191bddc831d3de66f5cae378343ce9c1\n\n## Summary\n\nThis PR wires an operator-approved reviewed batch into the existing daemon while leaving the normal single-PR path and train publisher in place. The handoff does not preserve the approved head pins, and the new preparation step can publish a local-main history that is not telemetry-only. Both require changes before deployment.\n\n## Findings\n\n<!-- findings:begin -->\n- [ ] F1 **S4/C5** `local/bin/daemon_train.py:98` - The pinned SHA is checked only against the earlier scan; `run` then hands `pr_train.py` PR numbers alone (lines 99-102). If PR #580 advances from approved pin A to a different independently green/reviewed head B after that scan and before the train claims its members, `pr_train.members_at` obtains B through `pr_merge.run_gate` (`local/bin/pr_train.py:90-105,306-311`) and integrates B, even though the operator's JSON authorized A. A fixture probe with an old scanned pin and a subsequently green B admits B. The train's current-head gate verifies B's evidence, but does not verify that B was the requested head. Fix: pass the requested PR-to-SHA mapping into the train, validate it under member claims against the gate results, and retain its check through the publication verifier; refuse if any pin changed.\n- [ ] F2 **S3/C5** `local/bin/daemon_train.py:86` - `_base_advance_is_tolerated` checks the net tree difference, not every unpublished commit. In an offline primary fixture, commit a change to `README`, then commit its reversal: `github/main..main` contains two nontelemetry commits but its net diff is empty. The predicate returns true and `prepare_primary` reaches `github-sync.sh main` (line 89), publishing that history despite the documented telemetry-only-local-lead restriction. Fix: verify each unpublished commit's changed paths/modes against the passive-telemetry allowlist before calling `github-sync.sh`; keep a nontelemetry history as an operator reconciliation case.\n<!-- findings:end -->\n\n## Verification Limits\n\n- Read the full six-file 403-line PR patch, complete changed files, trusted-main review/protocol instructions, the train/merge/sync/claim implementations, and all three hash-pinned runtime inputs. The three runtime SHA-256 digests and six source SHA-256 digests match the supplied receipts.\n- Seven adapter tests pass locally. One earlier combined invocation ran 34 tests without test failures but exited 1 because I specified nonexistent `test_pr_merge_freshness`; the seven adapter tests were rerun independently and pass. The offline F1 and F2 fixture probes reproduced their stated paths. `git diff --check` passes. The patch applies to a temporary copy with `--fuzz=0` and passes `bash -n`; its preview SHA-256 is `ba1702939e2a5f07daec40f3662d90be203cb32d0b2819cbfb3e4ea4d4086071`.\n- The exact-head CI, author receipt, normal commit hook and rooted audit are published evidence, not proof of these untested edge cases. No live train, daemon installation/restart, production primary publication, full hook suite, or Lake build was run by this reviewer. The historical 507/579/592 contract and issue 589 recovery scope were not reopened.\n\nVERDICT: CHANGES_REQUESTED\n", "state": "COMMENTED", "html_url": "https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-A/pull/595#pullrequestreview-5244965776", "pull_request_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-A/pulls/595", "author_association": "OWNER", "_links": {"html": {"href": "https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-A/pull/595#pullrequestreview-5244965776"}, "pull_request": {"href": "https://api.github.com/repos/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-A/pulls/595"}}, "submitted_at": "2026-09-18T06:40:43Z", "commit_id": "00e2079fb16f665721bf6b0fb209f07d22e0906f"}, "statuses": {"local-ci/summary": {"state": "success", "description": "all gating steps passed (410s)", "created_at": "2026-09-18T06:21:20Z"}, "local-ci/statement-origin": {"state": "success", "description": "passed in 0s", "created_at": "2026-09-18T06:21:08Z"}, "local-ci/proof-evasion": {"state": "success", "description": "passed in 47s", "created_at": "2026-09-18T06:21:06Z"}, "local-ci/proof-debt": {"state": "success", "description": "passed 